'Correct source-verified false current codec claims in reviewed paper artifact.\nLegacy numeric trials are retained with local-harness/attempt-channel labels.\n'
import sys,json,re
from pathlib import Path
from docx import Document
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'experiments'));import paper50 as P
p=ROOT/'paper/MEGA27-23b-50p.docx';d=Document(p);changes=[]
def replace(index,needle,text):
 old=d.paragraphs[index].text;assert needle in old,(index,needle,old)
 d.paragraphs[index].text=text;changes.append({'paragraph':index,'before':old,'after':text})
replace(13,'Existing codecs','Screening rejects candidate oligos that violate chosen constraints before synthesis. It is not itself an inner error-correcting code, but published DNA Fountain includes Reed-Solomon inner protection and its port exposes configurable parity. The implemented never-same differential decoder has local substitution effects at two adjacent trits, not catastrophic suffix propagation. Indels are a different unvalidated channel.')
replace(16,'Unique contribution','Scoped contribution: executable local constrained codecs, audited channel/checksum/resource-accounting limits, and a separate in-model flux reallocation identity. Code density is measured on encoded bases. No validated physical mapping connects that density to a living host metabolic cost; a combined empirical optimization remains open.')
replace(23,'biologically admissible','We model specified software constraints, not biological admissibility. Continuous never-same mapping prohibits adjacent repeated bases; blocked v2 can repeat bases at seams. GC bounds are measured statistics, not guaranteed synthesis success. Historical rates are attempted changes with expected realized probability 0.75 p; new audits use strict changed-base probabilities. Indels, physical synthesis and read consensus remain outside the present validation.')
replace(29,'attains this bound','The three-choice transition alphabet has asymptotic no-adjacent-repeat capacity log2(3). Mapping one trit to each permitted successor realizes that alphabet, but the implemented byte conversion uses six trits for eight bits. It therefore carries 4/3 payload bits per body base before headers/checksums/copies, below capacity. The complete codec is not capacity-achieving byte packing.')
replace(30,'desynchronization','5. Substitution locality and full-strand detection')
replace(31,'every subsequent','The decoder computes t_i=(idx(s_i)-idx(s_(i-1))-1)mod 4 from observed adjacent bases. A substitution at position i changes only trit i and the next trit if present. Later pairs contain unchanged observed bases and decode normally. Invalid spacing or a whole-message checksum can reject a strand, but that is detection, not suffix corruption.')
replace(32,'E[f_corrupt]','(3) For one substitution at position i, changed decoded trits are a subset of {i,i+1}.')
replace(33,'tends to1' if False else 'tends to 1','The previous formula for a suffix-corruption fraction is withdrawn. Source-level local dependence and exhaustive 2880 single-base events agree that no downstream trits change. Historical recovery collapse does not establish the claimed propagation mechanism.')
replace(35,'bounds desynchronization','Blocked v2 partitions 32 payload trits with six checksum trits and restarts the differential mapping from a block-index seed. This supports local block rejection and parity repair, not a needed cure for downstream substitution propagation. Seam bases may repeat, so continuous HP1 guarantee does not automatically cover the joined blocked strand. No physical synthesis tolerance is established.')
replace(36,'6-trit checksum','The block stores checksum_trits(payload)[-6:]. Because each Fletcher byte is encoded as six trits, this retains only the low byte s1 modulo 255 and discards the s2 byte. It has at most 255 possible values, not a uniform 729-value checksum.')
replace(37,'3^-6','(4) No distribution-free checksum collision probability is established. Equal-and-opposite trit changes can preserve the retained s1 checksum.')
replace(49,'faithful Goldman','Historical local-harness trial design: v1, blocked v2, an unscrambled never-same Goldman-style approximation and a uniform-low-degree CRC8 Fountain-style approximation. These are not faithful implementations of the published methods. CRC8 detection is not equivalent to their Reed-Solomon correction. Attempt-rate labels realize expected 0.75 p. The archived 24-message trial tables remain historical outputs; source-pinned external clean-valid audits later in the paper replace superiority interpretation, not their data.')
replace(52,'highest recovery','The retained historical v2 trials recover more messages than these local controls at several attempted-error rates. Their exact table values are unchanged. The invalid-clean Fountain-style control and mismatched noise/resource semantics prevent a published-method superiority or fair frontier inference. Later external-port parity sweeps show how parameter allocation can reverse the pilot ranking.')
replace(54,'Density-improvement','Historical two-copy sensitivity remains a local attempted-rate observation. Copy disagreements, detection and parity limits can cause file rejection. Those outputs do not establish a universal redundancy requirement or optimum, and the codec family has not been compared under matched physical constraints and complete copy/read accounting.')
replace(58,'strictly dominates','The historical RSNS rate sweep measures local software configurations, not strict domination of published codes. Its original attempted-rate tables are retained. Source-pinned clean-valid external parity audits and segmented local controls show that density, geometry, sequence constraints and parity allocation change the ordering. Published-codec superiority remains withdrawn.')
replace(74,'The verdict asks','Published-family comparisons require the actual implementation, stated channels, matched constraints, geometry and budgets. Earlier claims that Fountain has no inner correction or that its measured deficit certifies local superiority are withdrawn. The pinned external port includes RS parity and its clean-valid RS24 configuration outperforms the segmented local pilot at strict 2%substitution while allowing HP5 rather than HP1. Archival, biological synthesis and host-resource equivalence remain untested.')
replace(111,'asymptotically independent','An ideal uniformly sampled three-choice never-same chain has stationary GC fraction 1/2, but successive GC indicators are not independent. The actual deterministic scrambler and six-trit byte mapping also need not realize that ideal chain. A binomial window variance or independent-window extreme-value approximation therefore cannot be used as a verified law for this implementation. Empirical GC statistics are retained separately.')
for index in [118,120,124,126]:
 old=d.paragraphs[index].text;replace(index,'The desynchronization mechanism dominates its failure curve.',old.replace('The desynchronization mechanism dominates its failure curve.','Historical attempted-channel output; no suffix-desynchronization mechanism or faithful published-codec equivalence is established.'))
replace(166,'wasted synthesis','External screening rejects candidates computationally before synthesis. The number of rejected candidates affects encoder effort, not necessarily synthesized-base cost. Accepted fraction depends on sequence length, parity, payload and screen settings; no universal 70-80%acceptance or wasted-synthesis inference is established. The fixed-budget graph audits quantify actual accepted droplets and attempts for their configurations.')
replace(476,'Two properties matter','The v2 block check is the low Fletcher byte s1, not the full Fletcher pair. Equal-and-opposite trit errors preserve it, so correlated checksum collisions exist. A zero observed collision count in a finite trial is not proof of a distribution-free bound. Explicit counterexamples and emitted-length accounting are in results/codec_rate_checksum_audit.json. Whole-message checks and block parity are separate safeguards and do not make the low-byte check a uniform hash.')
replace(503,'2 bits per base','The implemented conversion carries 8 bits per 6 trits. With c identical copies, continuous v1 emits c(6 L+24) bases for L payload bytes. Blocked v2 emits c*38*(ceil((6 L+24)/32)+1) bases: 32 payload and 6 check trits per block, plus one parity block. These are exact implementation lengths, excluding primers and external indexing.')
replace(504,'2 B','(11) lim R_v1=4/(3 c); lim R_v2=(4/3)*(32/38)/c. For c=3: 0.444444 and 0.374269 bits/encoded nt.')
replace(505,'2B','The previous 2 B/(B+1) rate formula is withdrawn: a no-adjacent-repeat stream has only three successor choices, and the implementation also uses inefficient fixed six-trit byte packing. Headers, checksums, parity blocks and copies are charged by the exact formulas above. No primer budget was included in these local encoded-base rates.')
replace(516,'Error floor','Checksum collision limits, not an error-floor theorem')
replace(517,'worst case' if False else 'A parity block','A checksum collision probability requires a specified distribution over corruption patterns. Low-byte Fletcher collisions include deterministic equal-and-opposite trit changes. There is no proven universal exponential floor or worst-case suppression with checksum length in this implemented block check.')
replace(518,'3^{-(L-1)}','(15) Worst-case undetected corruption can occur; a universal 3^(-(L-1)) bound is not established.')
replace(38,'Errors are thus','Detected invalid blocks are treated as erasures. If exactly one payload block is known erased, all other payload blocks are correct and the parity block is correct, the tritwise parity equation reconstructs it. Undetected corruption and a bad parity block are outside that conditional guarantee.')
replace(41,'vote fails','The event that at least two of three independent copies have a changed base has the following Bernoulli probability. For four-letter substitutions, this event is not identical to vote failure: two erroneous letters can differ, and tie handling matters.')
replace(42,'p_vote','(6) P(at least two changed copies)=3*p^2*(1-p)+p^3. It is not a validated exact base-vote failure formula for the implemented tie rule.')
replace(43,'Tier 2','The implementation first attempts a voted block, then retries single copies and attempts one-erasure parity repair. Acceptance depends on differential invalid-spacing checks and the low-byte checksum, which can miss correlated trit errors. These dependent events do not establish the earlier independent-block failure calculation.')
replace(44,'P(fail)','(7) The earlier union-bound numeric claim is withdrawn pending a correct conditional block-error model.')
replace(45,'10^-4','Even under the earlier stated surrogate expression, q=1-(1-0.000298)^38+0.32^3 gives q about 0.04403; choosing two of 15 blocks gives about 0.2036, not 10^-4. This arithmetic contradiction invalidates using that expression as agreement with observed recovery. Actual trial recovery remains an empirical local-harness result.')
replace(47,'keystream is uniform','The SHA256 counter keystream is deterministic and reduces digest bytes modulo three, which gives residue zero 86 of 256 values and each other residue 85. It is not exactly uniform or independent random noise, and a fixed scrambler does not guarantee uniform output for every payload. Empirical strand GC statistics are observations, not a theorem of binomial window fluctuations or biological manufacturability.')
replace(511,'Goldman-2013','Published methods use different framing, replication and indexing conventions. The local unscrambled approximation does not reproduce the published Goldman redundancy protocol, so an effective published rate cannot be inferred from the following unverified formula.')
replace(512,'R_G','(13) Published Goldman density under matched complete accounting is not established by this local harness.')
replace(513,'expected overhead','Fountain decoding overhead depends on degree distribution, screening, source-chunk count, seed coverage and the decoder. The near-matched clean audit shows that a full-rank matrix can still stall peeling.')
replace(514,'E[n_LT]','(14) No universal 5-10 percent overhead guarantee is established for these screened finite-message configurations.')
replace(515,'At nonzero','Historical local baseline failures and source-pinned external trials are retained separately. Invalid clean recovery is a benchmark gate failure, not a meaningful noisy comparison. Current file recovery is reported with actual parameters and complete encoded-base accounting.')
replace(507,'With c independent','With c independent copies and per-base survival q, the binomial tail below is the probability that a strict majority are correct. For odd c this is sufficient for correct voting, but not necessarily identical to implemented plurality success when incorrect votes split.')
replace(509,'quantitative basis', 'For three copies, at least two correct bases guarantee a correct vote; the complementary event does not invariably make the vote wrong. A per-position strict-majority probability is not full-message success, and cannot justify the observed five-copy recovery without a joint strand and decoder analysis. The earlier claimed quantitative explanation is withdrawn.')
P.save(d,str(p));(ROOT/'results/codec_paper_claim_corrections.json').write_text(json.dumps(changes,indent=2)+'\n');print('corrected',len(changes),'paragraphs; historical numeric tables retained')
